	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The authors used the “random forest algorithm on Cox modeling” and the R package “RandomForestSRC” to calculate variable importance for 1-year mortality. Recipient and donor tabular variables from UNOS were included. A complementary Cox model was used to verify findings, so the comparator is best classified as Other. I did not find a reported train/test split, cross-validation scheme, SHAP/LIME-style interpretability, or hyperparameter tuning. Variable selection was clinically/manual in the sense that variables “known to be associated with risk of mortality after OHT” were included, with high-missingness variables excluded.

